{
  "case_id": "2010-09-291",
  "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 704(a), Title VII, prohibits the use of third-party reprisals as a method of retaliating against a person who complained to the EEOC or otherwise opposed discrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first requirement is that the plaintiff show that discrimination occurred with regard to the individual who engaged in a protected activity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is Ms. Regalado still engaged to this fellow?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could she have gotten reinstatement on the grounds that his continuing inability to be employed by the company is an ongoing hurt to her?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The question is whether he's aggrieved within the meaning of Title VII, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When an employer fires an employee as a means of retaliating against a relative or close associate who has filed an EEOC charge, the employee who has been fired is entitled under Title VII to go to court and seek appropriate remedies, even if he hasn't himself engaged in protected activity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So why don't we get to the second question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Latherow",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. LATHEROW: Yes, I -- I believe it should be read into Title VII, because that's the term\n\"aggrieved.\"\nIf someone -- if my husband calls and says,\noh, my gosh, we've been involved in a car accident, I\ndon't say: Honey, are you aggrieved? I say: Honey,\nare you injured? And that's exactly -- exactly the\ndefinition of \"aggrieved\" in the Fair Housing Act.\nSo Congress recognized, just 4 years later\nafter Title VII was adopted, when it enacted the Fair\nHousing Act, and it defined \"aggrieved\" and said\naggrieved means or includes any person who claims to\nhave been injured."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: It doesn't have to do with the evidence in a particular hearing. Can a person who is a close relative sue on the grounds that he was injured, deliberately so, in order to retaliate against his spouse or his fianc\u00e9e?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Latherow",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He says in this memo: I am\ndisappointed in compensation this year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-291",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "87541634de577cea230a777a9cc40b23c0bb26ff1b4ba5b9a9cf3688526bca97",
      "evidence_id": "ev-87541634de57-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you. Thank\nyou, counsel.\nThe case is submitted."
    },
